Cantonal flags of Switzerland
  Limen/Resources/Assets.xcassets/flag-*.imageset
  Source: Wikimedia Commons
  Licence: Public domain

  Twenty-six cantonal flags, retrieved from Wikimedia Commons and bundled verbatim from the same
  files the Android app ships. Each one is recorded in cantons-manifest.json with its Commons
  title, original URL, source page, SHA-256 and credit line, so any one of them can be traced
  back to what was downloaded.

  Most derive from the Swiss Confederation's Reglement 51.340 d, "Der Umgang mit Fahnen,
  Standarten und Fanions".

  These flags identify cantons only and do not imply official endorsement. Rules on the use of
  official symbols may apply independently of copyright: in Switzerland the Coat of Arms
  Protection Act (WSchG, SR 232.21) governs cantonal arms, and public-domain status under
  copyright is not permission to use a cantonal coat of arms as a badge of authority.
